# Supabase for this repo

The hosted project is `grelplmmgywqoliqzrfi` (`grelplmmgywqoliqzrfi.supabase.co`). Schema lives in `supabase/migrations/`. Do not ask the user to paste SQL in the dashboard when you can apply it yourself.

## Preferred: Supabase MCP

If the `supabase` MCP server is connected (see `.cursor/mcp.json`):

1. Write or update the migration file under `supabase/migrations/`.
2. Call MCP `apply_migration` (or `execute_sql` for one-off repair) against this project.
3. Confirm with `list_migrations` / `list_tables` / a targeted `execute_sql` read.

If MCP status is `needsAuth`, authenticate once via Cursor Settings → Tools & MCP (browser OAuth). Do not put access tokens in the repo.

## Fallback: CLI

```bash
npx supabase db push
```

Requires a prior `npx supabase login` and `npm run db:link` on this machine. Never run `db reset` against the hosted project.

## Rules

- Keep DDL in versioned migration files; do not apply schema only through the dashboard.
- Do not commit `.env*`, service role keys, or personal access tokens.
- Seed (`supabase/seed.sql`) is intentional bootstrap only — never apply it as a casual follow-up to a feature migration.
